udiv16.asm adapts the unsigned split-division algorithm in SDCC
4.6.4 device/lib/z80-common/divunsigned.s, SVN revision 17147.
Upstream SHA-256:
c58c8b453e0944bbb91f2d335675cf3582a21b926a2450813941f396076e8207

The SM83 port replaces ADC HL,HL and SBC HL,DE with byte operations, uses
C to preserve A during the wide subtraction, replaces DJNZ with DEC/JR,
and maps the core result to the sangoku calling convention. The quotient
and remainder entries independently unpack their arguments. Division by
zero reaches RST $10. The core leaves quotient in BC and remainder in HL.

The original notice and additional exception follow. COPYING contains
the complete GNU GPL version 2 text.

