Copyright (c) 2021, Philipp Klaus Krause
Copyright (c) 2022, Sebastian 'basxto' Riedel <sdcc@basxto.de>

The four-bytes-per-iteration Duff's device loop is kept. The entry code maps
the sangoku calling convention (destination in BC, source split between A and
the stack, caller-popped arguments) onto it, and adds the backward copy that
memmove needs when the destination overlaps the end of the source. SDCC has no
SM83 memmove (its z80-common version uses LDIR and LDDR). The same GNU GPL
version 2 notice and special exception as for divunsigned.s above apply.

mulo128.asm adapts the bit-wise Horner multiplication algorithm in SDCC
device/lib/_mullonglong.c (64-bit generic implementation) to a 128-bit SM83
stack frame, with sticky carry tracking for unsigned overflow. The signed
wrapper converts operands to magnitudes, reuses the unsigned core, checks the
signed range, and applies the product sign.
